### The same calls as in the README, for IntelliJ IDEA Ultimate or the
### REST Client extension for VS Code. Start the application first:
###   ./mvnw spring-boot:run
### Send the requests from top to bottom: later ones use the monitor
### created by an earlier one.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Greeting
GET {{host}}/hello?name=Sanad

### List all monitors (contains the sample monitor, id 1)
GET {{host}}/api/monitors

### Check the sample monitor: the application calls its own /hello endpoint
POST {{host}}/api/monitors/1/check

### Create a monitor (it gets id 2)
POST {{host}}/api/monitors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Missing page",
  "url": "http://localhost:8080/no-such-page",
  "intervalSeconds": 60
}

### Get the new monitor
GET {{host}}/api/monitors/2

### Check it: the page does not exist, so it is down with status 404
POST {{host}}/api/monitors/2/check

### Replace it with a monitor that expects a keyword
PUT {{host}}/api/monitors/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Wrong content",
  "url": "http://localhost:8080/hello",
  "intervalSeconds": 120,
  "expectedKeyword": "Goodbye"
}

### Check it again: the page answers but lacks the keyword, so it is still down
POST {{host}}/api/monitors/2/check

### Delete it
DELETE {{host}}/api/monitors/2

### Invalid input: 400 with the reason for each field
POST {{host}}/api/monitors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "url": "example.com",
  "intervalSeconds": 1
}

### Unknown monitor: 404
POST {{host}}/api/monitors/999/check
